{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_69","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'tool.Disposition == \\\"not-used\\\"|case \\\"not-used\\\"|not-used.*rationale|Evidence.*not-used' pose-mcp/internal/pose/review* pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation*\"","aggregated_output":"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go:1956:\t\tcase \"not-used\":\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go:1964:\t\t\t\tblockers = append(blockers, \"required review tool \"+label+\" has no registered producer and still needs a not-used rationale\")\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go:1966:\t\t\t\twarnings = append(warnings, \"recommended review tool \"+label+\" lacks not-used rationale\")\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan_test.go:615:\tmissingRecommendedBody := strings.Replace(body, \"- assess-discover [not-used] component:api rationale:not-needed\\n\", \"\", 1)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_preflight_tie_test.go:44:\t\"has no registered producer and still needs a not-used rationale\":                                   \"`not-used` is accepted for a required tool only when the plan says no producer exists\",\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_preflight_tie_test.go:45:\t\"lacks not-used rationale\":                                                                          \"a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`\",\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go:268:\t\tif ok && t.Evidence == \"\" && (t.Disposition == \"deferred\" && containsString(tool.Preconditions, \"review-complete\") || t.Disposition == \"not-used\" && tool.Requiredness == \"recommended\") {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_conclusion_rules_test.go:35:\t\t\"recommended review tool lacks not-used rationale\":           {\"a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`\"},\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:87:const briefRulesTextV5 = \"POSE checks the conclusion before it records it, and refuses the whole draft when one rule breaks: (a) a `passed` criterion of kind judgment carries a `rationale` saying what you examined and what you concluded; (b) the `evidence` of a `passed` criterion is exactly one of the refs listed under Sealed evidence (`<class>:<id>`, of a class the criterion asks for when it names one), never a file and line, a command or a structural fact id: those go in a finding or in the `rationale`; (c) a criterion disposed `finding` carries as its `evidence` the `id` of a finding listed in `findings`, and that finding is open until you give it `action`, `owner` and `review_by`; (d) each structural fact listed above is answered by the criterion that asks for structural mapping, as its `mappings`: `[{\\\"delta\\\": <fact id>, \\\"basis\\\": <requirement or decision ref>, \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": <why>}]`, or `not-applicable` with the reason; (e) a `not-applicable` carries a `rationale` and is refused when the bundle seals evidence of a class the criterion asks for; (f) every required criterion and every tool above is answered; (g) the `disposition` of a tool is `passed`, `failed`, `not-used` or `deferred`, never anything else (`not-run` is refused); a tool listed as required must be run and `passed`, with the ref of the sealed evidence it produced as `evidence` when it names classes, and `not-used` is accepted for a required tool only when the plan says no producer exists; a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`; (h) the `evidence` of a tool is `<class>:<ref>`: when the tool lists evidence classes, a ref of one of them that the bundle sealed (listed under Sealed evidence), otherwise `command:` followed by the command you ran; a bare command line is refused; (i) a draft that approves leaves no finding open: each finding is either a follow-up with `action`, `owner` and `review_by`, which is recorded as an accepted risk, or the draft requests changes; a finding without them is open and the approval is refused.\"\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:102:\ttext = strings.Replace(text, \"a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`;\", \"a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`; a required tool whose precondition is the completion of the review (`review-check`, `closeout-check`) cannot pass before your attestation: answer it `deferred` with a `rationale`;\", 1)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
