{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_82","type":"agent_message","text":"The targeted tests passed in all three packages, and `go vet ./...` passed. The sweep found one new blocker: encoded link destinations can lose a real association in either direction without a diagnostic.\n\nBoth prior findings are fixed. The code/comment behavior remains a low-severity follow-up under the existing F6. The worktree is unchanged."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_83","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\n- **N48 — medium blocker:** [closeout_adr_associations.go:50](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3967574839/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go:50) silently drops encoded Markdown associations. For example, `../adr/decision%2Emd` and `../adr/decision&#46;md` name `decision.md`, but produce neither an association nor a diagnostic. Equivalent backlinks fail too. A two-member roadmap can consequently receive an incorrect exemption.\n- **N49 — low follow-up:** Code/comment examples and parentheses can require extra review or return unknown. This remains the accepted F6 over-enforcement risk.\n\nBoth prior findings are fixed. Targeted tests across domain, CLI and MCP passed; `go vet ./...` passed. Required artifact and surface commands exited 0. The repository remains unchanged.\n\nRules applied: mixed Go/governance feature; review workflow, backend-go, security, documentation-style, delivery-evidence and knowledge-governance.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N48\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go\",\n      \"line\": 50,\n      \"summary\": \"Decode Markdown destinations before testing the association namespace and extension, or report unsupported forms as unknown. The reader does not decode URL escapes or Markdown character references; it also truncates numeric character references at '#'. Thus '[decision](../adr/decision%2Emd)', '[decision](../adr/decision&#46;md)' and '[decision](../%61dr/decision.md)' all name the canonical decision.md but are silently skipped at lines 174-175. Equivalent backlinks to pair.md are skipped at lines 245-246. A read-only reproduction using the extracted production regex and namespace predicates confirmed associations=[] and diagnostics=[] for all six forward/backward cases. With two resolved members and no other association, evaluateCloseoutReview therefore returns Known=true and Required=false, violating R3. Normalize supported destination escapes before containment checks, or fail closed, and cover both association directions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N49\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go\",\n      \"line\": 43,\n      \"summary\": \"Existing spec follow-up F6 remains applicable: links shown in code or comments count as associations, and destinations containing parentheses return unknown even when a complete Markdown parser could resolve them. This can demand unnecessary review, but does not grant an exemption. Inspection and the passing TestCloseoutReviewPolicyRoundTwelve/RoundFourteen regressions confirm the conservative behavior; accept this limited over-enforcement risk.\",\n      \"action\": \"Complete existing spec follow-up F6 with context-aware Markdown parsing while retaining fail-closed behavior for unsupported or unresolved local associations.\",\n      \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-13\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R13-N46\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"closeout_adr_associations.go:42-64 no longer filters code or comments. TestCloseoutReviewPolicyRoundFourteen at closeout_review_policy_test.go:1604 covers both reported bodies in both association directions. Ran go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli ./internal/mcpserver -run 'Test.*CloseoutReview|Test.*CloseoutReceipt|Test.*ADRAssociation' -count=1; all three packages passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R13-N47\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"closeout_adr_associations.go:170-172 and 241-243 now diagnose destinations containing parentheses before extension filtering. TestCloseoutReviewPolicyRoundFourteen at closeout_review_policy_test.go:1630 covers forward and backward destinations and requires unknown rather than exemption. The targeted three-package test command passed.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed the spec R1-R7, D1/D2, accepted ADR, changed production files, schemas, manuals, templates and regression tests. Traced policy adoption and schema preservation; canonical member and transfer resolution; forward/reverse ADR metadata and Markdown parsing; protected baselines and mandatory-human requirements; voluntary-review vetoes; immutable receipt publication, interrupted roadmap recovery and historical verification. Inventoried CLI close, closeout-check, review-check, review verify, review-plan, attention/obligations, reached, nextCloses, roadmap-check, MCP closeout state, readiness/portfolio dependencies, federated acceptance and doctor. Checked their shared review/terminal paths and supporting member/cut-criteria gates. Ran required artifact-check and surface-check, suggest review, targeted three-package tests, go vet ./..., git diff --check and git status. Examined adversarial-corpus coverage and identified the uncovered encoded-destination exemption in N48. Used sealed full-validation evidence; did not run assessment/index/state writers or record an attestation. Final worktree status was clean.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Verified schema/default/legacy behavior and prior-finding fixes against code and independently rerun tests. Full validation is sealed producer evidence, not a claimed local rerun. Distinguished the unresolved R3 defect N48 from the conservative, owned F6 risk N49. Remote backlink discovery and protection against nonparticipating external writers remain outside the accepted design.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected guarded close, repeated authorization checks, ExpectAbsent receipt publication and intent/status/receipt sequencing. Existing coordination bounds remain in use; failures leave an incomplete close rather than overwriting a receipt.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Schema 5 explicitly migrates the aggregate policy contract while schemas 1-4 retain legacy semantics. CLI configuration requires the pair, MCP additions are projections, and receipt schema/path contracts are covered.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N48\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Traced CLI/MCP domain reuse, receipt-backed producer proof, canonical transfer destinations and aggregate dependency closure. The association defect is shared domain behavior, not transport divergence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N48\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-policy-adoption-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reviewed explicit adoption, legacy cutoffs and sealed-plan handling, schema-5 preservation in reference/transfer toggles, and previous-release compatibility tests. Older engines intentionally refuse fresh schema-5 instances; update does not adopt the pair.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N48\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-846b41e9a5123ab5\",\n      \"rationale\": \"D1 separates explicit aggregate closure from independent review using deterministic thresholds. D2 reuses the resolver, capability catalog and setup/adopt paths, adding receipts because milestone close previously had no persisted transition. Shared evaluation and receipt-backed terminal projection address inconsistent exemptions and closure claims; N48 identifies an implementation failure in association recognition.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-3ce6ee69\",\n          \"basis\": \"R4\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The explicit close delivery exposed the measured governance read-budget refusal. The spec's artifact reconciliation links the bounded 1-GiB amendment to completing close without truncating historical inputs.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-c74440ab\",\n          \"basis\": \"R3\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The roadmap template exposes adrs: [] for the explicit ADR associations used by when-justified.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-ec2d86f4\",\n          \"basis\": \"R1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The accepted ADR records policy location, deterministic modes, defaults, historical compatibility and authority protections before implementation.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared English/Portuguese manuals, scaffold copies and roadmap templates with runtime policy names, thresholds, adoption, explicit close and receipt behavior. The supported contract is documented consistently; N48 is its implementation defect, and F6 records conservative parser limitations.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N48\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N48\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared the declared artifacts and production changes with R1-R7 and D1/D2. Policy, receipt, reader, setup/doctor, schema and documentation changes support the approved aggregate closeout scope. No new MCP write tool or global ADR identity framework was introduced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N48\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-846b41e9a5123ab5\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A shared evaluator plus a write-once terminal receipt is sufficient for distinct review/close semantics; reusing adopt/setup/resolver avoids another configuration framework or global ADR type. Metadata alone would lose existing explicit Markdown associations. A narrow parser is sufficient only if unsupported local forms return unknown; N48 shows that condition is currently violated and needs correction. Remote backlink inventory remains deliberately excluded.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran the exact command; exit 0. Output included artifact.claims=46, artifact.observed=185 and artifact.findings=920 with provenance warnings. This is a successful gate exit, not a claim of warning-free global provenance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Did not rerun an assessment writer under the no-repository-changes boundary. Examined the design and structural mappings using sealed structure:design-846b41e9a5123ab5 and the current spec/ADR/code.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Did not regenerate component assessments. Inspected current component sources, validation registration and sealed pose-mcp evidence directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Did not run the assessment writer. Traced CLI/MCP/federation integration in code and examined sealed integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration plus independently rerun three-package tests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Did not write assessment artifacts. Inspected changed production markers and the spec's explicit follow-ups, including the bounded-read capacity debt and F6 parser limitations.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion gate requires the recorded review conclusion; no attestation was recorded during this independent review.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion gate must follow POSE recording and verifying this review conclusion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Exit 0; selected backend-go, security and documentation-style under the review workflow. Also applied delivery-evidence and consulted knowledge governance for residual-risk handling.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran pose surface-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict; exit 0 with surface.targets=1, surface.results=213 and surface.findings=0. Composition evidence: integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration. Reachability evidence: reachability:pose-mcp/go/closeout-plan-reachability. A passing surface gate does not cover the missing encoded-destination negative case N48.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Disposed from the sealed strict producer run, not rerun locally because validate writes repository results. Inspected delivery-validation.json: 213 checks, all pass. Independently reran the closeout-policy tests across pose, cli and mcpserver; all passed. go vet ./... also passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"build:pose-mcp/go/build\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The sealed strict run includes the component's registered build, unit, integration and e2e checks. Current targeted domain/CLI/MCP tests and go vet passed independently; the uncovered R3 parser case remains N48.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
